    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Nicholas Scott is an American hospitality businessman who leads Scott Enterprises in Erie, Pennsylvania. He expanded the hotel and restaurant business established by his father, a Greek immigrant. A Cornell University graduate, he works alongside his sons in a family enterprise whose properties extend across northwestern Pennsylvania and western New York.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "For hotelier Nick Scott, Splash Lagoon offered the chance to create a destination of his own instead of operating another franchise. Its indoor water park brought visitors to attached hotels in Erie and gave the family business an attraction that could draw guests throughout the year. His son Chris helped develop the project after studying water parks around the country.\n\nThe family's purchase of Peek'n Peak presented a different challenge: extending a ski resort's appeal beyond winter. Under Scott Enterprises, treetop adventure courses, zip lines and miniature golf joined the established slopes. The additions gave the property activities for warmer months while investment continued in its skiing facilities.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 85,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Interview and project history distinguish strategic perspective from son's development work."
    },
    "source_ids": [
